## 6. Login Panel Specification

### 6.1 Role cards

Three large cards, equal weight, each with an icon, a role title, and a one-line description.

| Card | Icon | Description |
|---|---|---|
| Patient | Smiling face | "Play, remember, and see your family" |
| Caregiver | Two people | "Set reminders and follow progress" |
| Healthcare Worker | Stethoscope or care icon | "Review patients and add notes" |

- Minimum height 88px, full width on mobile, selected state uses `--primary-tint` with a 2px `--primary` border and a tick.
- Tapping a card selects it and opens its entry area inline. Only one is open at a time.
- On a remembered patient device, the **Patient card is pre-selected and expanded**, and the other two are collapsed under "Not you?".

### 6.2 Patient entry

- Shows a large card: patient's photo (illustration placeholder), first name in 32px, and one big button "Continue as Ama".
- If no remembered profile, show a short list (max 4) of demo patient photo tiles, each tappable.
- **No typing, no password, no code.**
- Tapping a profile runs the mock login, shows a calm spinner for 300 to 600ms, and routes to `/patient`.
- Voice: "Hello Ama" plays after tap if voice is on.

### 6.3 Caregiver and Healthcare Worker entry

Fields:

| Field | Type | Rules |
|---|---|---|
| Mobile number | Numeric, 10 digits | Pre-filled with a demo number in demo mode. Inline message if shorter than 10 digits. |
| 4-digit code | Numeric, 4 boxes | Pre-filled in demo mode. Show/hide toggle. |

Actions:
- **Sign in** (primary, full width) with a loading state.
- **Need help signing in?** opens an inline help text ("Ask your healthcare worker or family member to share your code").
- Role-specific demo accounts, shown in a small "Demo mode" note: Caregiver (linked to Patient 1), Healthcare Worker (sees all patients).

Demo credentials (mock only):

| Role | Mobile | Code |
|---|---|---|
| Caregiver | 9000000001 | 1234 |
| Healthcare Worker | 9000000002 | 1234 |

In demo mode, any 4-digit code succeeds. A visible "Demo mode" chip makes clear this is not real authentication.

### 6.4 After sign-in

| Role | Route | First thing shown |
|---|---|---|
| Patient | `/patient` | Voice greeting, then pending reminders, then Home |
| Caregiver | `/caregiver` | Overview dashboard |
| Healthcare Worker | `/clinician` | Patient table sorted by "Needs attention" |

A "Switch role" link remains available in each professional view's settings so reviewers can return to `/`.

