## 7. States and Edge Cases

| State | Behavior |
|---|---|
| Page loading | Hero text renders first. Illustration lazy-loads with a soft placeholder. |
| Login loading | Button shows spinner and is disabled. Patient sees a single calm spinner. |
| Invalid mobile number | Inline plain message under the field: "Please enter all 10 digits." |
| Code does not match (non-demo) | Gentle message "That code did not match. Let's try again." Never "Invalid" or "Failed". |
| Empty fields | Sign in button stays enabled but shows inline "Please add your mobile number." |
| Offline | Page works. A small chip says "You are offline. You can still continue." Remembered profiles still sign in. |
| Voice blocked or unsupported | "Hear welcome" shows captions instead, with no error message. |
| Language font missing | Fallback to the nearest script font. Text always visible. |
| Unknown device (patient) | Show up to 4 demo profile tiles instead of a remembered card. |
| Permission denied (visiting a protected route while signed out) | Redirect to `/` with a short message "Please choose who is signing in." |
| Already signed in | `/` shows "Continue as {name}" at the top and a "Not you?" link. |
| Session ends (sign out) | Return to `/`, patient device stays remembered unless the caregiver clears it. |

**Patient safety rule:** the patient flow on this page has no dialogs, no errors, and no dead ends. If anything fails, show "Let's go home" with one large button that retries the patient's entry.

