## 8. Accessibility

- Role cards and buttons are keyboard focusable with a 3px `--blue` focus ring.
- The language toggle is reachable by keyboard and labeled for screen readers.
- Headline uses a single `h1`. Role cards use a `radiogroup` pattern with clear labels.
- Code inputs support paste, auto-advance, and screen reader labels ("Digit 1 of 4").
- Contrast meets WCAG AA minimum, and patient elements aim for AAA.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Captions appear for any audio.
- Touch targets: 64px minimum for patient elements, 44px minimum elsewhere.

---

## 9. Responsive Behavior

| Breakpoint | Layout |
|---|---|
| Mobile (under 640px) | Single column. Illustration sits between the headline and the role cards, scaled to 40% of viewport height. Buttons span full width. |
| Tablet (640 to 1024px) | Single column, larger type, role cards in a row if space allows. |
| Desktop (above 1024px) | Two columns. Hero on the left, login panel on the right, vertically centered. |

